---
title: "5 · Record payments"
description: Record full and partial payments received from the client, and delete a payment recorded in error.
sidebar:
  order: 6
  label: "5 · Record payments"
---

**Who:** any member who can see the invoice. Only managers can delete a payment. **Where:** the invoice page.

Operon does not collect payments online. When the client pays, for example by bank transfer, the payment is recorded on the invoice by hand.

## Record a payment

{% steps %}

1. Open the invoice and select **Record payment**. The page moves to the **Record payment** form under the paper.
2. **Amount paid (SGD)** is filled in with the amount still due. Change it for a partial payment.
3. Check **Date paid**. It is filled in with today's date.
4. Choose the **Method**: **Bank transfer**, **PayNow**, **Cheque**, **Cash**, **Card** or **Other**.
5. Optionally, enter the **Reference**, for example the bank reference.
6. Select **Record payment**.

{% /steps %}

The payment is added to **Payments and credit** and to the history, and the amount strip is updated:

- When part of the amount remains due, the status becomes **Partially paid**. The form stays open for the next payment, filled in with the rest.
- When nothing remains due, the status becomes **Paid** and the form closes.

For example, an invoice of S$1,979.99 with a payment of S$800.00 reads **Partially paid** with S$1,179.99 due. Recording S$1,179.99 makes it **Paid**.

No payment can be recorded on a draft, a void invoice, a credit note or an overpayment.

## The client paid more than the amount due

Enter the amount actually received. When it is above the amount due, the form says, under the amount, how much is above the amount due and that it will be kept as an overpayment for the client. Select **Record payment**: the payment is recorded for the amount due, the invoice becomes **Paid**, and the rest is kept as an overpayment. A payment above the amount due is always recorded this way; it is never recorded on the invoice for more than the amount due. See [Overpayments](/en/invoices/overpayments/).

## Delete a payment

A payment recorded in error is deleted by a manager.

{% steps %}

1. Under **Payments and credit**, find the payment and select **Delete payment**.
2. Confirm. The amount due goes back up and the status steps back, for example from **Paid** to **Partially paid**.

{% /steps %}

The deletion is kept in the history, with who deleted the payment and when.

When the payment left an overpayment, the confirmation says that the overpayment is voided as well. If any of the overpayment has been applied or refunded, the deletion is refused: remove those applications and refunds first.

{% aside type="note" title="Payments lock the amounts" %}
While a payment is recorded on an invoice, its lines and amounts cannot be edited, and it cannot be voided. The description, the footer note and the reference can still be changed. To correct the amount of an invoice that has been paid in part, a manager creates a credit note (see [Credit notes](/en/invoices/credit-notes/)).
{% /aside %}
